problems.problem:
These are artefacts of how the lab implemented each strategy, not properties of the strategies:
- the command undo has no existence guard (`m.get(id).x`);
- PropDiff's no-op on a deleted target is an explicit guard (strategies.mjs:292, `if (cur) ... // missing (deleted by someone else): skip`);
- each M case is a single scripted scenario (n=1).
Only the per-property granularity (M1) follows from the strategy itself.

The brief asks for [S]/[K] tags, but these numbers are untagged [K] or come from one prototype (n=1), and are presented as rules:
- up to about 8 independent decisions → one panel; 3–6 starting solutions;
- a 400–440 px panel; preview at 36–40 dvh (the prototype's single value);
- a 100–200 step cap; "at most two levels" behind More;
- undo top-left on desktop and bottom on phones (tldraw only; the prototype itself puts undo top-right on desktop).

Several items the brief names are thin or missing:
- comparison of variants gets no guidance, only "not tested";
- Nike By You yields no findings;
- snapping and guides are covered only as thresholds, with nothing on how guides are drawn or on distance labels;
- game character creators rest on one forum claim.
Also, a hostile or old link is repaired silently (heart + 50 people opens as round with no notice), which contradicts "never drop a choice silently".
